rsed Smiling Slasher Style might work. But then, I admit, that's just my preference, so don't take it as a knock on what you had!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T15:55:03-07:00","id":1209429,"title":"","content":"Seafaring Hero Style may also be practiced with a slashing sword or its artifact equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:09:50-07:00","id":1209442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209386-2e-what-tmas-use-slashing-swords-homebrew-accepted?p=1209429#post1209429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seafaring Hero Style may also be practiced with a slashing sword or its artifact equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I thought it was for wavecleaver daiklaves, auzhians, and such.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:13:03-07:00","id":1209446,"title":"","content":"Well to quote scroll of the monk<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seafaring Hero Style treatschain and rope weapons as form weapons. Practitioners may also use slashing swords or short swords or their artifact versions. </div> </div> </div>That said I generally don't recommend using Seafaring Hero Style as written, it was both quite weird and quite a few of its charms didn't work with the theme the style tried to evoce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T17:08:59-07:00","id":1209458,"title":"","content":"Great, someone I talked to for advice about how to make 'Smiling Slasher Style' as a TMA totally diverted from giving me advice, and is now working on [Some sort of serial killer style] as a CMA instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T18:19:41-07:00","id":1209464,"title":"","content":"Dont suppose anyone ever made versions of the Kamiya Kesshin Style have they?<br /> <br /> Hiten Mitsurugi is Celestial style obviously","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T16:35:00-07:00","id":1209810,"title":"","content":"Arbiter from the TMAs. As for CMAs, notably Violet Bier. Possibly 2.0's Cobra Style with two of them.<br /> <br /> Things get more interesting with Master's Hand Envisioned Anew. Tune Even Blade to short daiklaves, and all these and Fire Dragon become a deadly mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}